{{define "content"}}
<h1>Examples</h1>
<p class="lede">A couple of runnable snippets. The repository's
<code>examples/</code> directory has more — including
<code>the_works.crust</code> and <code>closures.crust</code>, which between
them exercise every keyword, operator, and builtin at least once.</p>

<div class="card">
  <h3>Hello, World</h3>
  <pre><code>deliver("Hello, World!")</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>Find a pair summing to a target (AoC 2020 Day 1 shape)</h3>
  <pre><code>recipe findPair(nums, target) {
    knead (i = 0; i &lt; slices(nums); i++) {
        knead (j = i + 1; j &lt; slices(nums); j++) {
            order (nums[i] + nums[j] == target) {
                serve [nums[i], nums[j]]
            }
        }
    }
    serve nobox
}

recipe store() {
    entries = ints(lines(unbox("input.txt")))
    pair = findPair(entries, 2020)
    deliver(pair[0] * pair[1])
}</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>Sets and for-each (AoC 2020 Day 6 shape — group answer union)</h3>
  <pre><code>recipe store() {
    groups = split(unbox("input.txt"), "\n\n")
    total = 0
    knead group in groups {
        answered = toppings{}
        knead person in lines(group) {
            knead ch in chars(person) {
                sprinkle(answered, ch)
            }
        }
        total += slices(answered)
    }
    deliver(total)
}</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h3>Grid neighbors, memoized Fibonacci, and the stdlib together</h3>
  <pre><code>cache = {}
recipe fib(n) {
    order (n &lt;= 1) { serve n }
    cache[n] = cache[n] ?: fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)
    serve cache[n]
}

g = grid("...\n.#.\n...")
knead pos in neighbors8((1, 1)) {
    deliver(pos, at(g, pos))
}

deliver(fib(30), gcd(48, 18), lcm(4, 6), pow(2, 10))</code></pre>
</div>
{{end}}
